cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "gpolish: post-draw layout and polish for Stata graphs, with gr2mpl, a Stata-to-matplotlib translator"
abstract: >-
  gpolish edits a Stata twoway graph after it is drawn: it labels lines at
  their ends, places point labels where they fit (with leader lines when a
  point is crowded), adds callouts, notes, arrows, braces and brackets, and
  colours legend labels to match their keys. Run with no subcommand, it makes
  the title bold and removes the y-axis line and tick marks. The result is still a Stata graph.
  gr2mpl redraws a Stata graph held in memory with matplotlib, including every
  gpolish edit. The repository includes a reproducible label-placement
  benchmark against Stata's mlabel(), labrepel, adjustText and ggrepel.
authors:
